# Suave skills (required)

Before implementing or editing code in this repo, **read the matching skill with the Read tool as your first action**. Do not rely on memory of prior chats. Catalog: `.cursor/SKILL-REGISTRY.md`.

## Required skill touchpoint

Every change must do one of: read and follow the skill; update it when behavior changes; propose a new skill (registry row); or attest it was checked and is still accurate.

| Work | Skill path |
|------|------------|
| Shared Laravel / named routes / Pint / Do-not list | `.cursor/skills/system-coding-standards/SKILL.md` |
| Deep Eloquent / N+1 / architecture / validation | `.cursor/skills/laravel-best-practices/SKILL.md` (+ mapped `rule/` and `rule/suave.md`) |
| New/edit Service | `.cursor/skills/create-service/SKILL.md` |
| New/edit Form Request | `.cursor/skills/create-form-request/SKILL.md` |
| New migration | `.cursor/skills/create-migration/SKILL.md` |
| Admin panel, RBAC, DataTables, admin CRUD | `.cursor/skills/suave-admin/SKILL.md` |
| Marketing site, assets, CSS, SuaveAgent | `.cursor/skills/suave-frontend/SKILL.md` (+ `reference.md` when renaming assets) |
| Broken images / URLs / sections audit | `.cursor/skills/frontend-audit/SKILL.md` |
| Branch / PR review | `.cursor/skills/code-review/SKILL.md` |
| After skill-affecting changes | `.cursor/skills/orchestration-maintenance/SKILL.md` |

If admin and frontend both apply, read **both** domain skills (plus `system-coding-standards`). After reading, follow those skills for the rest of the change.
